# Line-ending policy, declared once.
#
# Why this file exists: `core/.editorconfig` sets `end_of_line = crlf`, but the
# repository had no `.gitattributes`, so the working copy's line endings were
# decided by each machine's `core.autocrlf`. On Windows (`autocrlf = true`) the
# LF blobs are checked out as CRLF and `dotnet format --verify-no-changes`
# passes; on a Linux CI runner the same blobs are checked out as LF, which
# violates `end_of_line = crlf`, so `dotnet format` fails there. The first-ever
# CI run (PR #22) surfaced this. Declaring the policy here makes both
# environments agree instead of depending on local git configuration.
#
# `text=auto eol=crlf` normalises to LF in the repository and checks out CRLF
# everywhere, matching `.editorconfig`. Nothing here changes a single byte in
# the repository's history: the stored blobs are already LF, and `text=auto`
# keeps them that way.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Scripts and manifests that must stay LF: a CRLF shebang or line ending breaks
# them on Linux, and they are not C#/XML/MSBuild so `.editorconfig` does not
# govern them.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf

# Binary files: never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.dll binary
*.so  binary
*.pdf binary
*.snk binary
*.pfx binary
